  "worked_solution": "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the right by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-1}.$\n\n- Translate the result up by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-1}+2.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/900f5f6ea59dfcf4811ef56f59a01f4d4b1505b7c7384cacbda2ec5b5f408e9c.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=\\sqrt{x-1}+2.$",
